@*
===========================================================
ORANGE TENDER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
PAGE: Tendering / Retendering Rounds

DEVELOPER OWNER: Amal
MODULE: Sourcing Officer / Tender Management
TRELLO TASK: None — no dedicated Trello card
TRELLO URL: —

PURPOSE:
Show all tendering rounds of a tender and start a new round
when too few offers were received.

BUSINESS ACCESS:
Sourcing Officer

ROUTE: /SourcingOfficer/Tenders/Rounds/{id?}

FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION:
- List TenderRounds for the tender with invitation and
  distinct-supplier offer counts.
- POST New round: mark the current round Failed, create the
  next RoundNumber.
- Business rule service: minimum offers per round (3, or 2
  after the allowed failed attempts) — finalize the counting
  convention in code, not in the schema.

DEPENDENCIES:
Tenders, TenderRounds, TenderInvitations, Bids.

STATUS:
UI SCAFFOLD ONLY — BUSINESS LOGIC NOT IMPLEMENTED.

IMPORTANT:
No dedicated Trello card: listed under Amal’s Tender
Management module — confirm ownership with the team.
===========================================================
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Tendering / Retendering Rounds";
    ViewData["WorkspaceSection"] = "Tender Rounds";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Every tendering attempt of a tender, its invitations and the offers it received.";
}
<partial name="_PageHeader" />
<partial name="_ScaffoldNotice" />

<section class="ws-panel pg-panel" aria-labelledby="tbl-tendering-rounds">
    <div class="pg-panel-head"><h2 id="tbl-tendering-rounds">Tendering rounds</h2></div>
    <div class="pg-table-wrap">
        <table class="pg-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Round #</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Opens</th><th scope="col">Deadline</th><th scope="col">Invited</th><th scope="col">Submitted offers</th><th scope="col">Distinct suppliers</th><th scope="col">Outcome</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody><tr><td colspan="8"><partial name="_EmptyState" model='"Select a tender to see its rounds."' /></td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<aside class="pg-note"><strong>Retendering rule</strong><p>Normally 3 submitted offers from 3 different suppliers are needed in the current round. With fewer, close the round as failed, start a NEW round and select/invite suppliers again from scratch. Earlier rounds and their offers stay recorded and are never counted in the new round. After three unsuccessful tendering attempts the approved exception permits proceeding with at least 2 offers from 2 distinct suppliers — a permission, not automatic advancement. Whether the initial round counts among the three is still to be confirmed (spec §21).</p></aside>

<partial name="_ConfirmAction" model='new ConfirmActionModel("Start a new tendering round", "Open the next attempt for this tender.", "Creates TenderRound N+1 with no invitations. Previous rounds and their offers stay unchanged.", false, false)' />
